/*****************************************************************************
    loopBranchT -- bare `break` / `continue` / `return` INSIDE LOOPS.
    Written 2026-07-31 as the regression net for the bare-return fix, and it
    covers ground nothing else in the tree did.

    WHY IT EXISTS. The bare-return ruling says an action's value is the value of
    the last executed statement, and the obvious implementation -- have the
    block hand back the PRIOR statement's value instead of the branch keyword
    node -- would have silently broken `break` and `continue`.

    THE MEASUREMENT THAT SHOWED IT: the VALUE and the BRANCH SIGNAL ride the
    SAME NODE. aCTionBrancH stamps isBranch (1=break, 2=continue, 3=return) on
    the node it returns, and FOUR loop handlers read that flag back off the
    body's returned value --
        aCTionWhilE  ruleActions.rtn  ~line 1002
        aCTionDO                      ~line  270
        aCTionFOR                     ~line  517
        (and the block's own `if result && isBranch break;`)
    -- so substituting a different node for the value drops the signal with it,
    and every loop silently runs to completion instead of breaking.

    NOTHING IN THE TREE COVERED THAT. This file is the baseline: capture it
    BEFORE the fix, keep it green AFTER.

    SENTINEL AT THE FOOT (standing harness rule H2).
*****************************************************************************/
Start();
include(unitTests);
include(utilities);

search reset stack Grokking UnitTests Utilities list;

register(LoopBranch);
define
    bqLoop;
    bqSum;

    /*  bare break: sum 0+1+2 then stop at 3 -> 3  */
    bareBreak code={
        bqSum = 0;
        bqLoop = 0;
        while bqLoop < 9;
            if bqLoop > 2;
                break;
            bqSum += bqLoop;
            ++bqLoop;
        return bqSum;
        };

    /*  bare continue: bqLoop increments FIRST, so it takes 1,2,3,4,5 and skips
        3 -- sum = 1+2+4+5 = 12. (An earlier draft of this comment said 8. That
        was MY arithmetic, not the language's; the measured 12 is correct and
        `continue` works. Recorded because a fixture with a wrong expectation is
        worse than no fixture -- it manufactures a defect.)  */
    bareCont code={
        bqSum = 0;
        bqLoop = 0;
        while bqLoop < 5;
            ++bqLoop;
            if bqLoop == 3;
                continue;
            bqSum += bqLoop;
        return bqSum;
        };

    /*  bare return OUT of a loop: must stop the loop AND the action  */
    bareRet code={
        bqSum = 0;
        bqLoop = 0;
        while bqLoop < 9;
            bqSum += bqLoop;
            ++bqLoop;
            if bqLoop > 2;
                return;
        };
    ;

print "1 bare break in while    ->[" bareBreak() "]  (want 3)":;
print "2 bare continue in while ->[" bareCont() "]  (want 12)":;
bareRet();
print "3 bare return out of loop -> bqLoop =[" bqLoop "]  bqSum =[" bqSum "]  (want 3 / 3)":;

print "LB SENTINEL -- run reached the end":;
stop();
